<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ollantaytambo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ollantaytambo is a town and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> archaeological site in the Sacred Valley of the Urubamba, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. It was a royal estate of the Inca ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pachacuti">Pachacuti</a>, with temples, terraces and a fortress of fitted stone, and in 1537 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manco-inca">Manco Inca</a> defeated a Spanish attack there. Its town still preserves its Inca street plan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ollantaytambo.jpg" alt="Ollantaytambo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FLASHPACKER TRAVELGUIDE · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ollantaytambo_-_Heiliges_Tal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
